  "title": "Governance as code: CODEOWNERS, ruleset JSON and the repository-settings audit",
  "status": "done_with_deviations",
  "summary": "Adds `.github/CODEOWNERS` (D6), ruleset bodies `.github/rulesets/{main,tags,tag-creation}.json` built from `required-checks.json`, `bin/repository-settings-audit.php` (offline fixtures and `--live`) with `tests/Arch/RepositorySettingsAuditTest.php`, and a RELEASING.md section with the exact apply, audit and break-glass commands.",
  "why": "P0-A (A01): rulesets applied by hand drift; the audit requires an API-level check of rulesets, required checks, tag protection and bypass actors. Risks: a required context that no job produces blocks every PR (rule S7 catches it); `required_approving_review_count` > 0 deadlocks a single maintainer (D1); gh calls through a shell string allow injection — use argv arrays.",
